#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Emit the GitHub Pages landing page for the apt repository, to stdout.
#
# The Pages artifact is the entire site, so this page is what a visitor to
# https://berg.github.io/ugpibd/ sees. Its whole job is to hand over the
# copy-pasteable setup snippet.
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'HTML'
<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>ugpibd apt repository</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body {
    max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem;
    font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .sub { opacity: 0.7; margin-top: 0; }
  pre {
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto;
    background: #f4f4f5; border: 1px solid #e4e4e7;
  }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.9em; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #e4e4e7; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    pre { background: #1c1c1f; border-color: #2e2e33; }
    th, td { border-color: #2e2e33; }
  }
</style>

<h1>ugpibd apt repository</h1>
<p class="sub">
  Userspace daemon for USB-GPIB adapters, with HiSLIP and Prologix TCP
  front-ends. &middot;
  <a href="https://github.com/berg/ugpibd">source</a>
</p>

<h2>Install</h2>
<pre><code>sudo install -d /etc/apt/keyrings \
  &amp;&amp; sudo curl -fsSLo /etc/apt/keyrings/ugpibd.asc \
       https://berg.github.io/ugpibd/apt/ugpibd-archive-keyring.asc \
  &amp;&amp; echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/ugpibd.asc] https://berg.github.io/ugpibd/apt stable main" \
       | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ugpibd.list &gt;/dev/null \
  &amp;&amp; sudo apt update \
  &amp;&amp; sudo apt install -y ugpibd</code></pre>

<p>
  The key is registered with <code>signed-by=</code>, so it is trusted for this
  repository only rather than system-wide.
</p>

<details>
  <summary>deb822 <code>.sources</code> form, if you prefer it</summary>
<pre><code>sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ugpibd.sources &gt;/dev/null &lt;&lt;'EOF'
Types: deb
URIs: https://berg.github.io/ugpibd/apt
Suites: stable
Components: main
Architectures: amd64 arm64
Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/ugpibd.asc
EOF</code></pre>
</details>

<p>
  The service does not start on its own. Set <code>UGPIBD_AUTOSTART=yes</code> in
  <code>/etc/default/ugpibd</code> to start it when an adapter is plugged
  in, or run <code>sudo systemctl enable --now ugpibd</code> to start it at boot
  regardless of hardware. See <code>man ugpibd</code>.
</p>

<h2>Packages</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Package</th><th>Contents</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>ugpibd</code></td>
    <td>The daemon and the <code>ugpibd-scpi</code> client, udev rules, systemd units.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>ugpibd-blacklist-linux-gpib</code></td>
    <td>
      Optional. Blacklists the kernel GPIB drivers, for when they claim the
      adapter first &mdash; the symptom is
      <code>failed to claim interface 0</code>.
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Supported distributions</h2>
<p>
  <code>amd64</code> and <code>arm64</code>, for Ubuntu 22.04 and later, Debian 12
  and later, and 64-bit Raspberry Pi OS. The packages depend only on glibc 2.34
  or newer, since the USB layer is pure Rust with no libusb. There is no
  <code>armhf</code> package; 32-bit Raspberry Pi OS needs a build from source.
</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    Every published release stays in the pool, so a specific version can be
    installed with <code>apt install ugpibd=&lt;version&gt;</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    The <code>Release</code> file carries no <code>Valid-Until</code>, so the
    repository does not expire between releases.
  </li>
  <li>
    Individual <code>.deb</code> files are also attached to each
    <a href="https://github.com/berg/ugpibd/releases">GitHub release</a> if you
    would rather not add a repository.
  </li>
</ul>
HTML
